[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent reference-expression and control audits

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-REFERENCE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Value-only reference expression reconstruction
STATEMENT: >>>
The physical audit shall reconstruct supported expression values without using
the production AD evaluator or Jacobian. Manufactured load states shall balance
for every supported operator against independent analytical values, and fail
when the supplying current is perturbed. Invalid domains shall not become zero
values or passing physical checks.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: audit_reference_contracts every_reference_operator_and_nonzero_control_terminal_obeys_independent_values
and reference_domains_fail_without_substituting_a_zero_or_passing_audit.
Implementation: audit.rs reference_expression, dc_currents and constraint_checks.
Finite operator cases do not establish universal floating-point accuracy.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-REFERENCE-LIMITS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve public expression structure limits
STATEMENT: >>>
Public audit entry points shall validate expression structure before reference
evaluation. An expression at depth 64 or exactly 1024 nodes shall remain
admissible when other inputs are valid. Depth 65 or 1025 nodes shall be rejected
as InvalidInput before independent reconstruction.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: public_validation_and_reference_evaluation_agree_at_exact_structure_limits.
Source path: audit public entry -> validate_state -> Circuit::validate -> Expr::validate.
Configured source overrides preserve expression trees. Counter mutations in a
private reference traversal may be redundant only under this current validation
invariant; retain original raw outcomes and inspect each diff. Do not remove
defensive guards or add broad mutation filters on the basis of that observation.
This source-path assessment is not a formal proof or a future API guarantee.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-CONTROL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Signed control difference is independent of common-mode voltage
STATEMENT: >>>
Behavioral resistance, VCCS and voltage-scaled CCCS physical audits shall use V(cp)-V(cn), including
nonzero negative control terminals. Translating both control potentials by the
same offset shall preserve their load currents and physical audit outcomes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: every_reference_operator_and_nonzero_control_terminal_obeys_independent_values,
18 expression forms and three control offsets with analytical source currents.
Voltage-scaled CCCS verification uses voltage_scaled_cccs_uses_signed_differential_control_and_sensed_branch_current
with a separately loaded sensing source and known signed branch current.
These finite states do not qualify arbitrary nonlinear circuit convergence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-GMIN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Add explicit shunt current to signed physical currents
STATEMENT: >>>
For an explicitly regularized audit, each node shunt current Gmin*V(node) shall
be added to its signed physical current sum. A current state balancing the
regularized circuit shall pass, while omitting the nonzero shunt supply current
shall fail. Non-unit valid Gmin values shall obey the same rule.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: explicit_nonunit_gmin_is_added_to_physical_node_currents.
Manufactured 2 V source and 2 ohm load use three explicit shunt conductances.
Regularized physics is not evidence for the unregularized circuit.
<<<
